val23=L'algorithme d'Euclide donne:<br>	<span class="red">$val9</span>= \($val17 \times )<span class="red">$val10</span>+<span class="orange">$val15</span><br>	\($val10= $val16 \times $val15+)<span class="green">$val13</span><br>	\($val15= $val14 \times $val13+)<span class="blue">$val11</span><br>	\($val13= $val12 \times $val11+1)<p>	  On obtient les coefficients de Bezout en remontant l'algorithme:</p>	\(1= )<span class="green">$val13</span>\( - $val12 \times )<span class="blue">$val11</span><br>	\(1= )<span class="green">$val13</span>\( - $val12 \times )(<span class="orange">$val15</span>\( -$val14 \times) <span class="green">$val13</span>)\(=(1+$val12 \times $val14))<span class="green"> $val13</span>\( -$val12 \times)<span class="orange"> $val15</span><br>	\(1= $val18 \times )<span class="green">$val13</span>\( - $val12 \times)<span class="orange"> $val15</span>\(= $val18 \times)(<span class="red">$val10</span> \(-$val16 \times) <span class="orange">$val15</span>)\( -$val12 \times) <span class="orange">$val15</span>\(= $val18 \times )<span class="red">$val10</span>\( - ($val18 \times $val16 +$val12) \times)<span class="orange"> $val15</span><br>	\(1= $val18 \times )<span class="red">$val10</span>\(- $val19 \times )<span class="orange">$val15</span>\(= $val18 \times) <span class="red">$val10</span>\( - $val19 \times) (<span class="red">$val9</span> \( - $val17 \times )<span class="red">$val10</span>)\(= ($val18+ $val19 \times $val17) \times) <span class="red">$val10</span>\( - $val19 \times) <span class="red">$val9</span><br>	\(1= $val20 \times) <span class="red">$val10</span>\( -$val19 \times) <span class="red">$val9</span>
